# secrets — never commit
.env*
*.key
*.pem
.secrets*
*_SECRET*
*_API_KEY*
# ...but not test MODULES about secrets. core.ignorecase=true (the macOS default) makes
# *_SECRET* match test_secrets_arms.py, which git then drops from a bulk add SILENTLY.
# Filename patterns cannot judge content anyway; gitleaks scans contents and is the real guard.
!tegh/**/test_*.py
# python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
venv/
*.egg-info/
build/
dist/
# written by a local rehearsal of the release workflow's consumer-lock step
release/
.venv-*/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
# Only the Claude Code harness reference is published. The references for
# harnesses tegh does not wrap yet are not published and stay in a working
# checkout.
docs/references/harnesses/*
!docs/references/harnesses/claude-code.md
